What is a Virtual Proxy?

A Virtual Proxy delays the creation of an expensive object until it is actually needed (Lazy Initialization).

Example:

Loading a large image
Connecting to a database
Loading a PDF
Creating a machine learning model

Instead of creating the heavy object immediately, we create a lightweight proxy. When the client calls a method, the proxy checks if the real object exists:

If No → create it.
If Yes → reuse it.